detail: Nothing under app/ moved, so both my tasks are untouched. On the three points: (1) every commit on echo-opus-bt1 was made with 'git -C <worktree>', never 'cd <repo> && git commit', so the jurisdiction fix changes nothing about how mine are judged. (2) Noted on the <sha12>.<teammate>.ack key; this ack is written by the script, not by hand. (3) g7 is directly relevant and my check does NOT borrow the operator's pointer: gui-launch.sh creates the engine pointer at <scratch-home>/.claude/richos-engine inside a mktemp -d HOME, never at ~/.claude. Verified just now: ~/.claude/richos-engine -> /Users/alex/ab/richos/engine, intact and not dangling. Separately, residue is ZERO — 'pgrep -f richos-tauri' returns 0. The 157 were mine: gui_boot killed the subshell instead of the app because 'cd / && env ... &' makes $! the subshell. Fixed in f41c837 with exec, a verify-after-kill gui_kill, a pid ledger and an EXIT/INT/TERM trap, plus three asserted cases (Y1 TERM path, Y2 KILL escalation for a process that ignores TERM, Z the launched-vs-still-running count printed every run). Measured over three consecutive runs: 18 apps launched, 0 still running, count 0 before and after.
